From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 20:54:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] context: rebind busy surfaces by default

Decoding into a surface whose CAPTURE buffer is still busy waits until
the decoder has caught up, which drains the queue to a single frame for
clients that hand surfaces back as soon as they leave the DPB. Allow up
to four spare CAPTURE buffers by default, so such a surface is decoded
into an idle buffer instead. V4L2R_REBIND=0 restores the wait.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 src/v4l2_request.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/v4l2_request.h b/src/v4l2_request.h
index c301198..bbed0ee 100644
--- a/src/v4l2_request.h
+++ b/src/v4l2_request.h
@@ -67,7 +67,7 @@ static inline uint64_t v4l2r_now_ns(void)
  * count plus the pipeline depth, so keep headroom up to the 64-bit bitmask. */
 #define V4L2R_MAX_CAPTURE_BUFFERS	64
 /* Spare CAPTURE buffers a busy surface may be rebound to (V4L2R_REBIND). */
-#define V4L2R_REBIND_DEFAULT 0
+#define V4L2R_REBIND_DEFAULT 4
 #define V4L2R_REBIND_MAX 8
 
 /* Upper bound on any single wait for the hardware (buffer/request/fence). */
